{"id":"word:hebrew:H4682","type":"word","title":"מַצָּה","subtitle":"H4682 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, sweetness ; concretely, sweet (i.e. not soured or bittered with yeast); specifically, an unfermented cake or loaf, or (elliptically) the festival of Passover (because no leaven was then used)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מַצָּה (H4682) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 53 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מַצָּה (matstsâh) means properly, sweetness ; concretely, sweet (i.e. not soured or bittered with yeast); specifically, an unfermented cake or loaf, or (elliptically) the festival of Passover (because no leaven was then used) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 23 29."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מַצָּה","transliteration":"matstsâh","pronunciation":"mats-tsaw'","strong":"H4682","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4682","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["מַצּ֖וֹת","הַ/מַּצּ֔וֹת","הַ/מַּצּ֛וֹת","הַ/מַּצּ֖וֹת","מַצּוֹת֙"],"morphs":[["HNcfpa",30],["HTd/Ncfpa",16],["HNcfsa",4],["HC/Ncfpa",2],["HC/Rd/Ncfpa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, sweetness ; concretely, sweet (i.e. not soured or bittered with yeast); specifically, an unfermented cake or loaf, or (elliptically) the festival of Passover (because no leaven was then used)","usage":"unleaved (bread, cake), without leaven.","full":"H4682. matstsah I. מַצָּה noun feminine unleavened bread, or cake(s) ; — absolute ׳מ Lev 2:5 ; 8:26 ( מ ׳חַלַּת אַחַת ), Num 6:19 ( id. ), 6:19 ; usually plural מַצּוֺת Exod 12:15 44 t.; מַצֹּת 12:18 3 t; — unleavened bread , prepared in form of לֶחֶם 29:2 ; חַלָּה 29:2 4 t. P; רקיקים 29:2 ; 1Chr 23:29 4 t. P; עגּה Exod 12:39 ; used at ordinary meals (prepared hastily): מ ׳אפה Gen 19:3 (J), Exod 12:39 (J), 1Sam 28:24 ; probably also Judg 6:19-20 , 21 (twice in verse); elsewhere at sacrificial meals, e.g. ritual peace-offerings Lev 2:4 (twice in verse); 2:5 ; 6:9 ; 7:12 (twice in verse); 10:12 ; consecration of priesthood Exod 29:2 (3 t. in verse); 29:23 ; Lev 8:2 , 26 , 26 ; at peace-offering of Nazirite Num 6:15 (twice in verse); 6:17 , 19 (twice in verse); at Passover Exod 12:8 ; Num 9:11 (all P); especially at feast of unleavened bread [ cakes ] for 7 days after Passover המ חג ׳שׁמר Exod 23:15 (E), 34:18 (J); מ ׳שׁסר 12:17 (P), (ה)מ ׳חג עשׂה 2Chr 30:13 , 21 ; 35:17 ; Ezra 6:22 ; המ ׳בחג Deut 16:16 ; 2Chr 8:13 ; המ ׳חג ׳לי Lev 23:6 . During these seven days all Israel ate מצות Exod 12:15 , 18 , 20 (P), 23:15 (E), 13:6-7 , 34:18 (J), Lev 23:6 ; Num 28:17 (P), Deut 16:3 , 8 ; Josh 5:11 ; Ezek 45:21 . &#8212; 2Kin 23:9 read probably מִצְוֺת or מִנָיוֺת for ׳מ ᵑ0 ( אכל ); so Gei Kue Kmp Bu. [ מָצֻק ] see מָצוּק below II. צוק [ מְצֻקָה ] see מצוּקָה below I. צוק [ מֻצֶ֫קֶת ] see ׳מוּצ below יצק . מֵצַר see I. צרר . מצר (√ of following)","rootNote":"from 4711 in the sense of greedily devouring for sweetness;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 23 29","keyReferences":["1Chr 23 29","1Sam 28 24","2Chr 8 13","2Chr 30 13","2Chr 30 21","2Chr 35 17","2Kgs 23 9","Deut 16 3"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":53,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 23 29","book":"1Chr","chapter":23,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/מַּצּ֔וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncfpa"},{"reference":"1Sam 28 24","book":"1Sam","chapter":28,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מַצּֽוֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfpa"},{"reference":"2Chr 8 13","book":"2Chr","chapter":8,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/מַּצּ֛וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncfpa"},{"reference":"2Chr 30 13","book":"2Chr","chapter":30,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/מַּצּ֖וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncfpa"},{"reference":"2Chr 30 21","book":"2Chr","chapter":30,"verse":21,"englishText":"","source